// DAY 4 — LUNCHEON AND CARDS. The knock, a long luncheon on the terrace, then two of three: Jagu's pakhala (win his
// trust and he lets the kitchen key fall where you can find it), cards with the Raja, or Mrs. Ghatak's gossip.
// Gives: kitchen-key (with Jagu's trust; otherwise Night 4 has the coal chute). Clues: alibis, jagu-proverb.

scene "morning-4" day=4 place="breakfast" first="knock-4" name="Day 4 — Luncheon and Cards"

beat "knock-4" scene="morning-4" {
    line "narrator" "Knock. Knock. Knock. Then, unusually, a fourth, softer, as if Bhima had thought of something and decided against it."
    line "raja" "Luncheon on the terrace, Mr. Thistlewood! Jagu has outdone himself. Jagu always outdoes himself. It is the only thing he is afraid of." if="suspicion<=5" sound="laugh"
    line "raja" "Luncheon, Mr. Thistlewood. Sit by me. I like to watch a man eat." if="suspicion>=6"
    line "narrator" "The terrace: white cloth, silver, the heat standing on the marble like a guest who will not sit down. Mrs. Sahukar has a parasol and a fan and a smelling bottle, and uses all three."
    does resets="slots"
    go "hub-4"
}

beat "hub-4" scene="morning-4" {
    line "narrator" "The luncheon goes on. And on." if="slots<2"
    line "narrator" "The shadows have come round under the table. The Raja is asleep in his chair, with his mouth open and his rings on." if="slots>=2"
    choose "Eat Jagu's pakhala, and talk to Jagu." if="!ate-pakhala slots<2" go="pakhala" sets="ate-pakhala"
    choose "Play cards with the Raja." if="!played-cards slots<2" go="cards" sets="played-cards"
    choose "Sit with Mrs. Ghatak." if="!sat-mrs-ghatak slots<2" go="mrs-ghatak-4" sets="sat-mrs-ghatak"
    choose "Let the afternoon end." if="slots>=2" go="evening-4"
}

beat "pakhala" scene="morning-4" {
    does adds="slots"
    line "narrator" "Jagu the khansama brings you pakhala himself: cold rice in water, with a fried fish, a green chilli, and a pickle. He stands at your elbow, small and quick and terrified, while you eat it."
    line "jagu" "A guest who eats pakhala, sahib, is a guest who means to stay. My mother said so. A guest who means to stay should not ask questions in the kitchen."
    choose "\"The pickle is your mother's too, I think.\"" go="pakhala-right" regard=1
    choose "\"Excellent. What did you cook for the shikar party?\"" go="pakhala-wrong" suspicion=1
    choose "\"Delicious. My compliments.\"" go="pakhala-plain"
}

beat "pakhala-right" scene="morning-4" {
    line "jagu" "My mother's. Thirty years in a jar. Nobody has asked."
    line "narrator" "He takes away your plate. Under it, when he has gone, is a long iron key, which was not there before. Jagu does not look back." gives="kitchen-key" sets="jagu-trust" clue="jagu-proverb"
    go "hub-4"
}

beat "pakhala-wrong" scene="morning-4" {
    line "jagu" "Food, sahib. I cooked food. A cook cooks what he is given."
    line "narrator" "He goes so quickly the water in your bowl shivers. Across the terrace the Raja has noticed, and goes on noticing." clue="jagu-proverb"
    go "hub-4"
}

beat "pakhala-plain" scene="morning-4" {
    line "jagu" "Sahib is kind. A kind guest should sleep at night, sahib. All night. Every night." clue="jagu-proverb"
    go "hub-4"
}

beat "cards" scene="morning-4" {
    does adds="slots"
    line "narrator" "Cards: the Raja, Mr. Sahukar, and you, for annas a point. The Raja cheats with tremendous openness. Mr. Sahukar lets him. Halfway through, you could win."
    choose "Lose, gracefully." go="cards-lose" suspicion=-2
    choose "Win." go="cards-win" suspicion=1
}

beat "cards-lose" scene="morning-4" {
    line "raja" "Ha! The Englishman cannot shoot and he cannot play. What can you do, Mr. Thistlewood?" sound="laugh"
    line "thistlewood" "Photograph, Your Highness. And lose."
    line "raja" "And lose! Bhima, the man is a philosopher. Give him a cigar." sound="laugh-long"
    go "hub-4"
}

beat "cards-win" scene="morning-4" {
    line "narrator" "You lay down the winning hand. There is a pause long enough to boil an egg in."
    line "raja" "So. You can play, when you want to. I shall remember what you want to do, Mr. Thistlewood." sound="laugh-long"
    go "hub-4"
}

beat "mrs-ghatak-4" scene="morning-4" {
    does adds="slots"
    line "mrs-ghatak" "You are interested in the shikar party, Mr. Thistlewood. Everybody is interested in a party they were not invited to."
    line "mrs-ghatak" "We all went to bed at midnight. Pitambar says so. Dibakar says so. Lilabati says so, when she is conscious."
    line "mrs-sahukar" "I was in bed by ten. I had a headache. I always have a headache."
    line "narrator" "Mrs. Sahukar swoons, on cue, onto Mr. Sahukar, who catches her without looking up from his cards. Mrs. Ghatak watches him catch her. Her eyes are closed; she watches anyway." clue="alibis" sound="flutter"
    go "hub-4"
}

beat "evening-4" scene="morning-4" {
    line "narrator" "Dinner is a boar, roasted, carved by the Raja himself. Mrs. Sahukar does not eat. Mr. Ghatak eats twice, loudly, and talks about the medicinal relapse with his mouth full. Nobody looks at the meat."
    line "narrator" "Bhima bolts you in. Tonight: the servants' passage, the kitchens, the larder nobody opens, the walled garden where the fire was." sound="bolt-shut"
    ends "night"
}
